# Audit French originals first

Before translating a new original from `Originals/`, read that French PDF page by page and report inconsistencies. Do not start the English LaTeX until the user has seen the report.

Compare, at least:

- Summary unit tables versus that unit's description card (abilities, weapons, stats, morale, saves)
- Army lists versus profiles (contents, costs, command points, class)
- Named abilities used on a profile but missing, differently spelled, or differently valued in the special-rules text
- The same term or number written two ways in the French (typos, singular/plural, hyphenation)

Present each conflict as: entry, where it appears, what each source says. Ask which source to follow before translating those values.
